{"id": "EUVD-2026-75360", "enisaUuid": "544d9f54-9451-3c1e-b267-70ed7b2fb7eb", "description": "A flaw was found in crun. After pivot_root, reopening /dev/null for stdio can follow a symlink and attach a host file to container stdio, then change that file's ownership. Affected versions are crun 1.29.1 and earlier. Default configurations that mount a fresh /dev are not exposed. No fixed release is available yet.", "datePublished": "2026-09-10T08:57:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-02T13:59:48", "baseScore": 5.6, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:C/C:N/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2026:71668", "https://access.redhat.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-88265", "https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2531224", "https://github.com/containers/crun/"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-88265", "GHSA-cwhr-hwj2-cjrp"], "assigner": "redhat", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "91d44798-2158-3ee8-9602-1d2558b15f33", "product": {"name": "Red Hat Hardened Images", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}, "product_version": "patch: 1.30-1.hum1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "63265543-15e4-3f84-a8c7-8feaf8e52bfd", "vendor": {"name": "Red Hat"}}], "isExploited": false}